      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "\ud83d\udcca Choosing Between SGLT2 Inhibitors and GLP-1 Agonists for Type 2 Diabetes"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Metformin remains the traditional first-line therapy, but guidelines increasingly support SGLT2 inhibitors or GLP-1 receptor agonists as co-first-line options, especially for patients with specific organ protection needs.",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "SGLT2 inhibitors",
            "link": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10455499/"
          }
        ],
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "guidelines increasingly support SGLT2 inhibitors or GLP-1 receptor agonists as co-first-line options"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "\ud83d\udccc Core Comparison"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "SGLT2 Inhibitors (e.g., Jardiance):",
                "list": [
                  {
                    "snippet": "Oral pill taken once daily."
                  },
                  {
                    "snippet": "Lowers A1C by about 0.7% to 1%."
                  },
                  {
                    "snippet": "Modest weight loss (1\u20133 kg) ."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "snippet": "GLP-1 Agonists (e.g., Ozempic):",
                "list": [
                  {
                    "snippet": "Mostly weekly injections (some oral options exist) ."
                  },
                  {
                    "snippet": "Lowers A1C by up to 1.5% to 2%."
                  },
                  {
                    "snippet": "Significant weight loss (4\u20136 kg)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Heart Failure: Best for reducing heart failure hospitalizations."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Kidney Disease: Slows chronic kidney disease progression."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Convenience: Daily oral pill with fewer GI side effects."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Cardiovascular Risk: Lowers risk of major adverse cardiac events."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Obesity: Preferred for prominent weight loss goals."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Higher A1C: Better at lowering overall blood glucose ."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "SGLT2 Inhibitors: Increased risk of urinary/genital yeast infections."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "GLP-1 Agonists: Gastrointestinal issues (nausea, vomiting, diarrhea)."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
